  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, a substantial +10.6% improvement over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is a major performance lever. However, we only have one data point for aggregation (avgpool). Uncertainty: it is unclear whether transformer-based aggregation captures inter-profile structure more effectively than simple averaging, which would be critical for all downstream multiprofile and multimodal experiments. This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly one variable—aggregation method (transformer vs avgpool)—while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and RNA encoder constant. It directly extends the strongest result and resolves a design choice that will inform every subsequent multiprofile configuration. Under a limited budget, this single-variable comparison is the most informative next step: it either confirms avgpool is sufficient (simplifying the search space) or reveals that transformer aggregation unlocks further gains (justifying its use in multimodal settings)."
}

